  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The Rucellai Madonna is the earlier of the two works by Duccio for which there is written documentation (the other is the Maestà of 1308–11).",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Rucellai Madonna",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rucellai_Madonna",
          "accessed": "2026-11-06",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "In 1889, however historian Franz Wickhoff compared stylistic choices between the Rucellai Madonna and Duccio's Maestà, and soon other critics agreed that Duccio had indeed painted the Rucellai Madonna.",
        "lead": "For three centuries it passed as a Cimabue:",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Rucellai Madonna",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rucellai_Madonna",
          "accessed": "2026-11-06",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Wherefore this work caused so great marvel to the people of that age, by reason of there not having been seen up to then anything better, that it was borne in most solemn procession from the house of Cimabue to the church, with much rejoicing and with trumpets, and he was thereby much rewarded and honoured.",
        "lead": "Vasari, who believed the panel was Cimabue's:",
        "source": {
          "author": "Giorgio Vasari",
          "title": "Life of Cimabue, in Lives of the Most Eminent Painters, Sculptors and Architects (trans. Gaston du C. de Vere)",
          "year": "1568",
          "readAt": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/25326/pg25326.txt",
          "accessed": "2026-11-06",
          "tier": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Given the bitter political enmity of Florence and Siena, the Florentine civic group's choice of a Sienese artist is noteworthy.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Rucellai Madonna",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rucellai_Madonna",
          "accessed": "2026-11-06",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      }
    ],
    "matters": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The members of the Laudesi met in the chapel to sing lauds, or Latin hymns praising the Virgin; an image of Mary provided a focus for those devotions.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Rucellai Madonna",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rucellai_Madonna",
          "accessed": "2026-11-06",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      },
      {
